<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kandy</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Senkadagala</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kandy is a city in the central highlands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>, beside an artificial lake. It was the capital of the Kingdom of Kandy, the last independent Sinhalese kingdom, from the late 15th century until the British took it in 1815. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temple-of-the-tooth">Temple of the Tooth</a>, housing the Buddha's tooth relic, makes it Sri Lanka's chief Buddhist pilgrimage centre and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p></div>
